### Findings (worst first) — all three fixed

**F1 — 310 cells (12.0 m²) of café/dining seating floor sealed shut.** `x 564–604, y 454–514 pt`.
Crop `w_11` → 12× zoom at `x[545,620] y[440,525]`: two columns of four four-tops plus a third column of four, all floor between and around them untinted while the surrounding aisle is green. This is **raw-reachable customer floor** (the drawing connects it on every side) with no wall, no counter, no staff side, no enclosed room, and a widest internal passage of 1.11 m — it was closed by the auto `FLORAL` disk (670,512 r=130), whose 12 pt bridge reaches 93 pt west and welded the 6–8 pt chair-to-chair gaps shut. Exactly the defect `inclusions.json` entry 4 already documents for the floral display tables, 20 pt further west. *Truth: green.* **Fix: inclusion `[552,444,614,524]`** (restores 770/770 raw-floor cells, reconnects to the main component). New guard point: `must [582,483]` — `False` before the fix.

**F2 — walk_truth had zero `must` points in aisles 19–33: the entire west wing.** Frozen Foods (19–20), pet/hardware (21–23), paper (24–25), HBA (26–31), baby (32–33) — 15 aisles, ~40% of the sales floor — had no coverage; `[178,480]` only pins the pharmacy-pickup end of aisle 29. This is the precise shape of the store-24 miss. I verified the wing is in fact correct (per-aisle corridor scans at x = 200/230/260 are green over their full length, and 12 west-wing labels probe at 0 pt), so it was a blind spot, not a live defect — but nothing would have caught a seal there. **Fix: 6 mid-length `must` points** (aisles 19, 21, 23, 26, 30, 33) placed deep inside each corridor, plus `[985,200]` for the Market perimeter frontage, which was also uncovered.

**F3 — no `must_not` inside the pharmacy dispensing room or the room east of the restrooms.** The pharmacy `[122,410,166,551]` is the store's largest enclosed room and had nothing pinning it shut; likewise the 618-cell enclosed service room at `x[782,818] y[430,500]` (the largest room pocket after the vestibule). **Fix: `must_not [145,480]` and `[800,465]`.**

